(5773273, 840375, 93283, '<td valign="top">Interesting perspective... I like it</td>', 'Interesting perspective... I like it', '2009-12-20 14:04:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773287, 840018, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks like a great place to explore.</td>', 'Looks like a great place to explore.', '2009-12-20 14:33:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773295, 839612, 83313, '<td valign="top">It is a little known fact that Mary Kay started out as a notorious bank robber in the 1930''s. Bonny &amp; Clyde were mere amateurs in comparison. Mary always did her robberies with class, however. It was important to always leave a positive impression with people. (She was an early inspiration to the young Martha Stewart) Her style and class became her downfall, however, when her (very stylish) high heels slowed her getaway from the First National Bank of Podunk, Wisconsin. The local police were right behind her as she sped out of town. Unfortunately, her sense of style proved her downfall again, as the police found the pink sedan made for an easy target.<br/> <br/>Mary Kay turned her life around in prison, becoming the makeup giant we know today. Of course, the pink car remains her trademark to this day, a reminder that even the worst in society can be reformed.</td>', 'It is a little known fact that Mary Kay started out as a notorious bank robber in the 1930''s. Bonny & Clyde were mere amateurs in comparison. Mary always did her robberies with class, however. It was important to always leave a positive impression with people. (She was an early inspiration to the young Martha Stewart) Her style and class became her downfall, however, when her (very stylish) high heels slowed her getaway from the First National Bank of Podunk, Wisconsin. The local police were right behind her as she sped out of town. Unfortunately, her sense of style proved her downfall again, as the police found the pink sedan made for an easy target. Mary Kay turned her life around in prison, becoming the makeup giant we know today. Of course, the pink car remains her trademark to this day, a reminder that even the worst in society can be reformed.', '2009-12-20 14:53:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773296, 839220, 83313, '<td valign="top">I love the concept you captured here. Unfortunately, the image comes off as very soft and grainy.</td>', 'I love the concept you captured here. Unfortunately, the image comes off as very soft and grainy.', '2009-12-20 14:56:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773388, 840406, 101306, '<td valign="top">georgeoud I almost feel as if I am there, an amazing clarity</td>', 'georgeoud I almost feel as if I am there, an amazing clarity', '2009-12-20 17:40:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773474, 840438, 77196, '<td valign="top">I love the concept and the title. But, for me, the execution just didn''t quite get there. Not sure why, but there are a couple of things that work against you with this composition. In the central 3 panes, you''ve chopped off the top of the "arch", yet at the bottom of each, the entire arch is present, plus some additional unidentifiable "stuff" - generally it is better to balance - if you chop the top, chop the bottom too. Also, IMO, the left and right of the three panels distract - especially the left, which appears like it has lots to look at but, upon closer examination, does not. Plus, the right 4 sections of the picture are approximately the same width, but the area to the left is about 1/2 again as wide. <br/>Again, I love the concept and the title. I also like that the porch could be in perfect condition, but the distortions in the center 3 panels makes it look to be in decay. 4</td>', 'I love the concept and the title. But, for me, the execution just didn''t quite get there. Not sure why, but there are a couple of things that work against you with this composition. In the central 3 panes, you''ve chopped off the top of the "arch", yet at the bottom of each, the entire arch is present, plus some additional unidentifiable "stuff" - generally it is better to balance - if you chop the top, chop the bottom too. Also, IMO, the left and right of the three panels distract - especially the left, which appears like it has lots to look at but, upon closer examination, does not. Plus, the right 4 sections of the picture are approximately the same width, but the area to the left is about 1/2 again as wide. Again, I love the concept and the title. I also like that the porch could be in perfect condition, but the distortions in the center 3 panels makes it look to be in decay. 4', '2009-12-20 19:55:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773480, 840261, 77196, '<td valign="top">Besides that this shot seems like a stretch for the challenge, there are some issues with the shot that the overall effect / impact do not overcome. The fairly extreme graininess, almost everything out of focus, a long leading line that exits the top of the photo for no apparent reason, the same with a fairly strong white line leading from the rightmost branch to nowhere. The cat''s paw batting at the ornament gives some sense of "cute", but just doesn''t overcome the distractions. 3<br/>You might try cropping about the paw''s width above the last knot on the tree, and maybe on the right side to just remove part of the rightmost branch (paw left 1/3 of shot, to tree trunk another 1/3, and rightmost branches the last 1/3. Just a thought.</td>', 'Besides that this shot seems like a stretch for the challenge, there are some issues with the shot that the overall effect / impact do not overcome. The fairly extreme graininess, almost everything out of focus, a long leading line that exits the top of the photo for no apparent reason, the same with a fairly strong white line leading from the rightmost branch to nowhere. The cat''s paw batting at the ornament gives some sense of "cute", but just doesn''t overcome the distractions. 3You might try cropping about the paw''s width above the last knot on the tree, and maybe on the right side to just remove part of the rightmost branch (paw left 1/3 of shot, to tree trunk another 1/3, and rightmost branches the last 1/3. Just a thought.', '2009-12-20 20:01:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773501, 840325, 99708, '<td valign="top">Oh so creepy...I like it!</td>', 'Oh so creepy...I like it!', '2009-12-20 20:33:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5773596, 839397, 47933, '<td valign="top">Well, it''s Ursula''s old barn. Nice shot.</td>', 'Well, it''s Ursula''s old barn. Nice shot.', '2009-12-20 22:53:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5775377, 840369, 83313, '<td valign="top">Rickety in the extreme. Good thing it''s not a far drop!</td>', 'Rickety in the extreme. Good thing it''s not a far drop!', '2009-12-21 13:04:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5775378, 840378, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks more urban in nature to me. I''ll have to take your word that this is a rural location. At 394 pixels, when you can use up to 800, the image is way too small. You could have gotten a lot more detail into this.</td>', 'Looks more urban in nature to me. I''ll have to take your word that this is a rural location. At 394 pixels, when you can use up to 800, the image is way too small. You could have gotten a lot more detail into this.', '2009-12-21 13:08:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5775381, 840403, 83313, '<td valign="top">Very <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=63398" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">NikonJeb</a>-ish in appearance, though I know it''s not his.</td>', 'Very  NikonJeb-ish in appearance, though I know it''s not his.', '2009-12-21 13:09:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5775383, 840435, 83313, '<td valign="top">I feel cold just looking at this. I''ll take the trailer. At least I can move that to a warmer climate.</td>', 'I feel cold just looking at this. I''ll take the trailer. At least I can move that to a warmer climate.', '2009-12-21 13:11:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5775388, 839862, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nothing a little bit of Elmer''s can''t handle. Once that''s taken care of, we''ll call in the folks from one of those HGTV house-flipping shows, and we''ll make a modest profit on it. (Make sure to describe it as "cozy".)</td>', 'Nothing a little bit of Elmer''s can''t handle. Once that''s taken care of, we''ll call in the folks from one of those HGTV house-flipping shows, and we''ll make a modest profit on it. (Make sure to describe it as "cozy".)', '2009-12-21 13:16:38.000000', NULL, 1),
