(5782707, 839397, 18367, '<td valign="top">Having seen this barn and knowing what it does look like I docked a few points off of my score as I honestly did not believe it met the "Rustic" aspects of the challenge.  I know I will be taken to task for my comments but I am quite prepared to stand by them. It is a nice image though.<br/> <br/>Ray</td>', 'Having seen this barn and knowing what it does look like I docked a few points off of my score as I honestly did not believe it met the "Rustic" aspects of the challenge.  I know I will be taken to task for my comments but I am quite prepared to stand by them. It is a nice image though. Ray', '2009-12-27 14:18:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5782814, 840429, 9114, '<td valign="top">LOL Something about it looks familiar?<br/>Cute how you spelled tripod, you jokester<br/>Debbi</td>', 'LOL Something about it looks familiar?Cute how you spelled tripod, you jokesterDebbi', '2009-12-27 18:06:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5783135, 840399, 60495, '<td valign="top">Wow Tom you are on a roll, very nice!</td>', 'Wow Tom you are on a roll, very nice!', '2009-12-27 22:09:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5783143, 840265, 112620, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone for voting and the kind comments on my first entry into DP Challenge.  There are many incredible photographers and artists participating on this site, and I look forward to subsequent challenges.  <br/> <br/>On this location once sat a huge mansion built in the 1800s.  It was sold to the Masons about 1920, and they converted it to a Masonic Hospital.  The property later came into the ownership of the town.  In the infinite wisdom of the political machine, the mansion was razed as well as all other structures, and water tanks were erected!<br/> <br/>This is not IR.  The original had been cropped and manipulated in both Lightroom and CS4.  Most of the mods are levels, curves, hue and saturation, and opacity settings for various layers.<br/> <br/>I agree with kleski - too much white.  This was a last moment decision, prodded by a friend, and I had only the time of day at hand to take some shots.  <br/> <br/>Once again thank you for you kind comments and votes!</td>', 'Thank you everyone for voting and the kind comments on my first entry into DP Challenge.  There are many incredible photographers and artists participating on this site, and I look forward to subsequent challenges.   On this location once sat a huge mansion built in the 1800s.  It was sold to the Masons about 1920, and they converted it to a Masonic Hospital.  The property later came into the ownership of the town.  In the infinite wisdom of the political machine, the mansion was razed as well as all other structures, and water tanks were erected! This is not IR.  The original had been cropped and manipulated in both Lightroom and CS4.  Most of the mods are levels, curves, hue and saturation, and opacity settings for various layers. I agree with kleski - too much white.  This was a last moment decision, prodded by a friend, and I had only the time of day at hand to take some shots.   Once again thank you for you kind comments and votes!', '2009-12-27 22:13:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5783289, 840402, 54645, '<td valign="top">Gave this a 7, very underrated.</td>', 'Gave this a 7, very underrated.', '2009-12-28 00:03:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(5783918, 839397, 60495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RayEthier:</b></div><hr/><i> Having seen this barn and knowing what it does look like I docked a few points off of my score as I honestly did not believe it met the "Rustic" aspects of the challenge.  I know I will be taken to task for my comments but I am quite prepared to stand by them. It is a nice image though.<br/> <br/>Ray </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I kind of agree, I am guessing the reason the door and windows got blacked out was to make it appear more abandoned and Like others have noted I think I like the original image better than the entry but still a Really a beautiful scene and nice image!</td>', 'Originally posted by RayEthier: Having seen this barn and knowing what it does look like I docked a few points off of my score as I honestly did not believe it met the "Rustic" aspects of the challenge.  I know I will be taken to task for my comments but I am quite prepared to stand by them. It is a nice image though. Ray   I kind of agree, I am guessing the reason the door and windows got blacked out was to make it appear more abandoned and Like others have noted I think I like the original image better than the entry but still a Really a beautiful scene and nice image!', '2009-12-28 13:17:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5786436, 839397, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful</td>', 'Beautiful', '2009-12-30 00:47:05.000000', NULL, 0),
